# CODEOWNERS - GH-316
#
# Designates required reviewers for paths that need a human in the loop
# before merging, per this repo's existing "human-reviewed PR" conventions
# (see docs/GITHUB-INTEGRATION.md, SECURITY.md, ADR-0002).
#
# IMPORTANT - this file alone does NOT block merges. GitHub only enforces
# these required reviews once "Require review from Code Owners" is ALSO
# turned on as a branch protection rule for `main`
# (Settings -> Branches -> branch protection rule for `main` -> check
# "Require review from Code Owners"). That toggle is a manual, repo-admin
# step this story deliberately does NOT flip for you - see
# docs/GITHUB-INTEGRATION.md for why. Until a human turns it on, this file
# is inert documentation of reviewer intent, not an enforced gate.
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern in the file wins, so keep broad patterns
# first and narrower/more sensitive ones below them.

# CI/release automation: a careless or compromised workflow edit can
# exfiltrate secrets, change what auto-merges, or alter what gets published
# as a release - always wants a human look.
/.github/workflows/ @CI-Till-Krempel

# This file itself: changing who's required to review should itself
# require the current owner's review (standard CODEOWNERS self-protection).
/.github/CODEOWNERS @CI-Till-Krempel

# Declarative repo-policy notes (intended branch protection / CODEOWNERS
# enforcement state for humans to apply by hand) - see
# docs/GITHUB-INTEGRATION.md and docs/CONFIGURATION.md ("GitHub auth axis").
/config/github_config.yaml @CI-Till-Krempel

# Network egress allowlist for the sandboxed dev/eval containers - widening
# what hosts agents can reach is a security decision, not a routine edit
# (see docs/SETUP.md and ADR-0002).
/config/net-proxy/ @CI-Till-Krempel

# .env templates: shape the defaults every new project copies in; a bad
# default here (wrong provider, unsafe default, leaked-looking placeholder)
# propagates to every setup that follows the wizard. (Real, populated
# `.env` files are gitignored and never reach this repo, so only the
# templates below are in scope.)
/.env.example @CI-Till-Krempel
/.env.local.example @CI-Till-Krempel
/.env.test @CI-Till-Krempel

# Release process and security-disclosure docs: changes here redefine how
# this project ships releases or handles vulnerability reports - process
# documents, not just prose.
/RELEASE.md @CI-Till-Krempel
/SECURITY.md @CI-Till-Krempel
